# FAQs
faqs:
  - question: How many downspouts does my home need?
    answer: "<p>Generally one for every 20-30 feet of gutter. A lot of older Albertville homes don't have enough downspouts — they overflow during heavy rain even when gutters are clean. Adding a downspout or two can solve the problem.</p>"
  - question: My downspouts dump water right by the foundation. Is that bad?
    answer: "<p>Yes. Water pooling against your foundation causes serious problems over time — cracks, leaks, settling. Extensions or underground drains should move water at least 4-6 feet away, farther if possible.</p>"
  - question: What size downspouts are best?
    answer: "<p>Standard 2x3 inch downspouts work for many homes, but 3x4 inch handle heavy rain better. Given how much rain Albertville gets, larger downspouts are often worth the small extra cost.</p>"
  - question: Can you add downspouts to my existing gutters?
    answer: "<p>Usually, yes. If your gutters are in good shape, we can add downspouts without replacing the whole system. It's often a cost-effective solution for overflow problems.</p>"
  - question: Why do my downspouts keep clogging?
    answer: "<p>Debris getting past your gutters. Gutter guards can prevent most clogs. We can also install strainers at the gutter-downspout connection or use larger downspouts that clog less easily.</p>"

